  c. transfer this contribution license and grant sublicenses through any
     number of tiers, including under commercial, proprietary, or other
     license terms chosen by the Licensor, with or without charging a fee.

You also grant the Licensor and recipients authorized by the Licensor a
perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free patent license to make, have
made, use, offer, sell, import, and otherwise transfer your Modification. This
grant covers only patent claims you can license that are necessarily infringed
by the Modification alone, or by its combination with the Software as submitted.

These grants cover only rights you own or are authorized to grant. Identify
third-party material and its terms in the submission. Do not introduce material
whose terms prevent these grants unless the Licensor has first agreed in
writing to a specific exception. You must obtain any necessary permissions
from an employer, co-author, or other rights holder before submission.

To the extent permitted by law, you consent to editing, combining, publishing,
and commercial use of your contribution as described above and agree not to
assert moral rights to obstruct those authorized acts. Nonwaivable rights and
legally required attribution remain unaffected.

The contribution grants survive termination of your rights under this license.
The Licensor has no obligation to merge, publish, maintain, support, or pay for
your submission. Rejection or non-use does not cancel your grants or excuse
submission of later Modifications. You may separately license your own original
contribution, but this does not grant you commercial rights to the Licensor's
code or to a combined version containing it.

