8. Breach and termination

If you breach an applicable condition, your permissions under this license
terminate automatically. You must stop the activities requiring those
permissions, including running and distributing affected copies, unless and
until your permissions are reinstated. You nevertheless have a limited
permission to make the copies, changes, and deliveries reasonably necessary
to correct the breach and submit required source; it does not permit ordinary
operation or redistribution to other users before reinstatement.

For your first period of noncompliance, permissions are automatically
reinstated if you correct all outstanding breaches, end unauthorized use,
satisfy section 4 for overdue Modifications, and remedy the consequences where
reasonably possible within 30 calendar days after you discover any of those
breaches or receive notice of any of them, whichever occurs first. Section 4's
delivery suspensions and lawful-disclosure exceptions also apply when curing
a breach. A period of noncompliance begins with the first uncorrected breach
and ends when all outstanding breaches have been remedied under these rules.
Any breach after reinstatement requires the Licensor's written reinstatement.
Reinstatement does not erase liability for earlier unauthorized acts.

Termination does not revoke compliant recipients' direct licenses, the rights
in contributions already granted to the Licensor, obligations already incurred,
or terms intended to survive, including sections 9 and 10. The Licensor cannot
terminate a compliant user's permissions merely by changing policy or offering
different terms for later releases.

